# OneSignal Provider

Manages the configuration of [OneSignal](https://onesignal.com) apps through
OneSignal's REST API: the apps themselves, their API keys, segments and
templates. Journeys, whose API is in beta, are not covered, nor is anything
that is not configuration, such as users, subscriptions and messages.

The provider is built for [OpenTofu](https://opentofu.org).

## Installation

Builds are served from the provider mirror at `https://opentofu.regulad.xyz/`,
under the address `registry.opentofu.org/regulad/onesignal`. Add the mirror to
the CLI configuration, after `direct`, so that every other provider still
comes from its registry:

```hcl
provider_installation {
  direct {
    exclude = ["registry.opentofu.org/regulad/onesignal"]
  }
  network_mirror {
    url     = "https://opentofu.regulad.xyz/"
    include = ["registry.opentofu.org/regulad/onesignal"]
  }
}
```

Then lock it from the mirror:

```shell
tofu providers lock -net-mirror=https://opentofu.regulad.xyz/ registry.opentofu.org/regulad/onesignal
```

## Authentication

The provider authenticates with an Organization API key, made in the
OneSignal dashboard's organization settings. It covers apps
and their API keys. Segments and templates are documented with an app's own
API key; each of those resources takes an optional `api_key`, which is
normally the `value` of an `onesignal_app_api_key` in the same configuration,
and falls back to the Organization key.

